  "question": {
    "text": "One end of a massless spring of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;and natural length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is fixed while the other end is connected to a small object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> lying on a frictionless table. The spring remains horizontal on the table. If the object is made to rotate at an angular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math> about an axis passing trough fixed end, then the elongation of the spring will be"
